{
  "dom_id": "step-q75586",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Determine if $v=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ is an eigenvector of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\nIf so, then what is the corresponding eigenvalue?",
  "worked_solution": "The eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-3v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Av=-3v,$ we conclude that $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =-3.$",
